      name: mci_ro_reg_rand_test
      desc: ""
      stage: ""
      tests:
      [
        mci_ro_reg_rand_test
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_sram_axi_jtag_access_collision
      desc: '''
Perform simultaneous accesses to the MCI sram controller from AXI and JTAG interfaces.
This test should trigger a `dmi_axi_collision_error`.
            '''
      stage: ""
      tests:
      [
        mci_sram_axi_jtag_access_collision
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_sram_error
      desc: '''
Perform a write through the MCI SRAM controller, followed by the double ECC error injection and RMW command.
Test should result in ECC error being raised and data inside SRAM should not be modified.
            '''
      stage: ""
      tests: [
        mci_sram_error
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_lcc_state_error
      desc: '''
Move OTP into unlocked state and check that Caliptra-ss is unlocked.
Inject invalid state into `otp_static_state` and verify that caliptra-ss becomes locked.
Release error injection and check that caliptra-ss is once more in unlocked state.
            '''
      stage: ""
      tests: [
        mci_lcc_state_error
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_lcc_state_error_to_locked
      desc: '''
Move OTP into unlocked state and check that Caliptra-ss is unlocked.
Inject invalid state into `otp_static_state`.
Request scrap transition or inject state_error, release error injection and check that
caliptra-ss is no longer unlocked and in the `DEVICE_PRODUCTION`.
            '''
      stage: ""
      tests: [
        mci_lcc_state_error_to_locked
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_lcc_manuf_to_non_debug
      desc: '''
Move life cycle state to `TRANSLATOR_MANUF_NON_DEBUG` or `TRANSLATOR_MANUF_DEBUG` state.
Either issue a SCRAP request or inject a state error, then verify that device lifecycle moved to `DEVICE_PRODUCTION`.
            '''
      stage: ""
      tests: [
        mci_lcc_manuf_to_non_debug
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mci_lcc_no_zeroization
      desc: "Set one of the `cptra_ss_FIPS_ZEROIZATION_PPD_i` or `ss_soc_MCU_ROM_zeroization_mask_reg` and make sure that OTP was not zeroized."
      stage: ""
      tests: [
        mci_lcc_no_zeroization
      ]
    }
    {
      name: mcu_axi_streaming_boot_test_rom
      desc: "This test instantiates an AXI memory perihperal and initializes it with a production MCU firmware binary. Software running on the MCU configures the I3C core to bypass mode and performs the recovery flow over AXI, reading data from the AXI memory and feeding it to the I3C core. The test checks if the recovery process is performed correctly and the new image gets activated"
      stage: ""
      tests:
      [
        mcu_axi_streaming_boot_test_rom
      ]
    }
